WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:04.640
What kind of scene needs to&nbsp;
be shot 20 different ways?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.640 --> 00:00:09.200
A big action setpiece? For "Thor: Love and&nbsp;
Thunder," it was something a little more&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.200 --> 00:00:15.200
emotional. Join us as we figure out what scene&nbsp;
was so hard to get right, and chase down what else&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:20.480
wound up on the cutting room floor. Warning:&nbsp;
spoilers for "Thor: Love and Thunder" ahead.

00:00:20.480 --> 00:00:24.400
Filmmaking can be complicated. Sometimes&nbsp;
what looks like a simple shot that lasts&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:28.160
just a few seconds can take days,&nbsp;
weeks, or months to get right.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.160 --> 00:00:31.840
Pickup shots will happen months or&nbsp;
weeks after a movie has wrapped, and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.840 --> 00:00:36.960
reshoots can sometimes take place weeks&nbsp;
after a movie is otherwise in the can.

00:00:36.960 --> 00:00:42.240
Movies that are technically complicated and filled&nbsp;
with post-production work and CGI shots, like the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.240 --> 00:00:48.080
latest MCU entry "Thor: Love and Thunder," are&nbsp;
sometimes broken down into hundreds upon hundreds&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.080 --> 00:00:53.120
of different shots. There's a reason it takes&nbsp;
months for some films to make it to theaters.

00:00:53.120 --> 00:00:56.720
"It's been an absolute disaster, but&nbsp;
that's just the way it is on my films."

00:00:56.720 --> 00:01:01.040
Between the retakes, rewritten scenes,&nbsp;
bits that end up on the cutting room floor,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.040 --> 00:01:04.400
and the fact that sometimes&nbsp;
studios will demand reshoots,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.400 --> 00:01:09.360
there are occasionally whole storylines that&nbsp;
can end up being lost in the editing process.

00:01:09.360 --> 00:01:12.720
In a recent interview with IndieWire,&nbsp;
actress Natalie Portman revealed that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.720 --> 00:01:16.240
director Taika Waititi shot&nbsp;
one particular moment in "Thor:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.240 --> 00:01:21.280
Love and Thunder" in 20 different ways.&nbsp;
Indiewire didn't say what scene it was,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.280 --> 00:01:26.320
possibly to avoid spoilers, but Portman&nbsp;
noted that it was very emotional, saying,

00:01:26.320 --> 00:01:29.680
"The interesting thing was how&nbsp;
we had room to workshop them.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.680 --> 00:01:36.000
We filmed 20 different versions of [one key&nbsp;
scene]. There's a few pivotal emotional scenes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:39.680
but we did really, really different&nbsp;
things, many different times."

00:01:39.680 --> 00:01:42.240
It's quite possible that she&nbsp;
was referring to one emotional&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.240 --> 00:01:46.960
part that involves Portman's Jane Foster&nbsp;
and Chris Hemsworth's Thor breaking up.

00:01:46.960 --> 00:01:48.000
"Quite a reunion, huh?"

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:52.720
Portman also described some scenes that were&nbsp;
deleted from the movie's final cut. The actress&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.720 --> 00:01:56.880
revealed later in the interview that certain&nbsp;
scenes with Tessa Thompson's Valkyrie and Jane,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:56.880 --> 00:02:00.960
which help explain Jane and Valkyrie's&nbsp;
friendship after Jane picks up Thor's mantle,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.960 --> 00:02:02.880
weren't included. Portman said,

00:02:02.880 --> 00:02:07.680
"There were whole sequences, planets,&nbsp;
characters, and worlds that didn't end&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.680 --> 00:02:13.600
up in the movie that were hilarious and amazing&nbsp;
and [that] we spent a lot of time and energy on,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.600 --> 00:02:17.200
and certainly the entire crew&nbsp;
also designing and conceiving."

00:02:17.760 --> 00:02:20.400
Seems like a director's cut may be in order.

00:02:20.400 --> 00:02:23.920
While we don't know for certain just&nbsp;
how many scenes were cut from "Love and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.920 --> 00:02:28.960
Thunder," we do know that at one point,&nbsp;
there was a four-hour cut of the film.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.960 --> 00:02:33.920
Taika Waititi and Chris Hemsworth spoke about&nbsp;
the cut to Collider, where Waititi explained,

00:02:33.920 --> 00:02:38.800
"It was about four hours. And a lot of time on&nbsp;
set. [...] in the moment, you're like, 'This is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.800 --> 00:02:43.600
the greatest thing that anyone's ever filmed in&nbsp;
the history of filming things.' And you get into&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.600 --> 00:02:49.440
the edit. You're like, 'I still kind of like it.'&nbsp;
And then, after about six months of it being in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.440 --> 00:02:54.880
the movie, you realize it was fun on the day but&nbsp;
it doesn't have any business being in the movie."

00:02:54.880 --> 00:02:58.560
What kinds of things could we expect&nbsp;
to see in a four-hour-long "Thor:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:58.560 --> 00:03:02.960
Love and Thunder?" According to Christian Bale&nbsp;
who plays Gorr the God Butcher, there were two&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.960 --> 00:03:08.320
previous MCU actors who made appearances that&nbsp;
wound up getting cut. Bale told Prensaescenario,

00:03:08.960 --> 00:03:14.080
"I got to work with Peter Dinklage. That's not&nbsp;
in the final film, but I got to work with him.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:14.080 --> 00:03:19.440
He's fantastic. I got to work with Jeff Goldblum.&nbsp;
He's not in the final film either. As you see,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:19.440 --> 00:03:24.560
a lot of stuff ends up on the cutting room floor&nbsp;
even though it is beautiful, brilliant stuff."

00:03:25.120 --> 00:03:29.920
It's unclear what kind of interactions Eitri&nbsp;
and the Grandmaster would have had with Gorr,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:29.920 --> 00:03:33.600
but it's a good bet things wouldn't&nbsp;
have shaken out too well for them.

00:03:33.600 --> 00:03:38.080
Thanks to a lawsuit currently in process, we&nbsp;
know actress Lena Headey had a role that was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:38.080 --> 00:03:42.960
ultimately cut, too. She's never appeared&nbsp;
in the MCU before, so it's unclear who she&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:42.960 --> 00:03:48.560
would've played. For our money, she would've made&nbsp;
an exceptional Hera against Russell Crowe's Zeus.

00:03:48.560 --> 00:03:51.360
One can only hope we'll see all of these&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:51.360 --> 00:03:56.640
unseen cameos one day. It would make&nbsp;
for some great bonus content on Disney+.

